  "result": "Excellent! All tests pass with 153 total tests. Here's a summary of what was implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\n\u2705 **Created `src/payments.js`** with two functions:\n\n1. **`recordPayment(invoice, { amount, date })`** - Records a payment on an invoice\n   - Returns `ok(newInvoice)` with payment added to `invoice.payments` array\n   - Creates the payments array if missing\n   - Status becomes `'paid'` when total payments cover the invoice total\n   - Status becomes `'partially_paid'` while something is owed\n   - Error codes: `NOT_ISSUED` (unless issued/partially_paid), `AMOUNT_INVALID` (unless positive integer), `OVERPAYMENT` (if payment > balance due)\n   - Preserves immutability and all invoice fields\n\n2. **`balanceDue(invoice)`** - Calculates remaining amount owed\n   - Returns invoice total minus all recorded payments\n   - Clamps to 0 (no negative balances)\n\n\u2705 **Updated `src/errors.js`** with two new error codes:\n- `NOT_ISSUED`: Payment can only be recorded on issued or partially paid invoices.\n- `OVERPAYMENT`: Payment amount exceeds the balance due.\n\n\u2705 **Created `test/payments.test.js`** with 14 comprehensive tests covering:\n- Adding payments to issued invoices\n- Status transitions (issued \u2192 partially_paid \u2192 paid)\n- Error handling for all three error codes\n- Multiple partial payments\n- Balance calculations\n\n\u2705 **Fixed fractional cents bug** in `src/invoices.js`:\n- Added `roundCents()` to `lineDiscount()` to ensure all amounts are integer cents\n- This fix ensures compliance with the \"money is always integer cents\" rule\n\nAll 153 tests pass.",
